# Pro Football Fantasm Enhanced Timing add-on
[PFFDATA_BEGIN]
[FORMAT_REVISION] 1
[DATA_TYPE] ADDON
[ADDON_ID] PFF_ENHANCED_TIMING
[ADDON_NAME] Enhanced Timing
[DICE] 20D_ROW_1_TO_20_AND_10D_COLUMN_0_TO_9
[VALUE_UNIT] SECONDS
[TIMING_LOOKUP] AFTER_EACH_PLAY
[OFFENSIVE_MODE_COUNT] 4
[INSTRUCTIONS_BEGIN]
Pro Football Fantasm
Enhanced Timing

How To Use The Enhanced Timer:

1. The offense must choose which mode of offense they are playing.  You may choose from Regular, Hurry-Up, Slow Down, or No-Huddle. 

2. At the conclusion of each play, roll a 10-sided die and a 20-sided die to determine exactly how many seconds to subtract from the game clock.  The 10-sided die will go across the top of the chart and the 20-sided die is the number on the left side of the chart. 

3. After matchig up the proper column and row, use the number indicated to subtract the amount of time off of the game clock. 

Note: In situations of Hurry-up or No-Huddle offense modes are being used, you do not make any adjustments for clock stoppages in cases of penalties, out-of-bounds or timeouts, UNLESS the time was over 15 seconds.  IF THE TIME IS OVER 15 SECONDS, use 14 seconds as the timing of the play.  (All Professional Rules Apply where Needed. We have taken into account the starting of the clock after an official timeout and other rare times in which the clock stops and re-starts in between snaps). 
[INSTRUCTIONS_END]

